{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/972693-changeling-the-lost-vampire-werewolf-mage-crossovers","id":972693,"title":"Changeling: The Lost/ Vampire/Werewolf/ Mage crossovers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T13:44:33-07:00","id":972693,"title":"Changeling: The Lost/ Vampire/Werewolf/ Mage crossovers","content":"I really like to see a Changeling 2e book that explores crossing Changeling with other supernatural titles. In Changeling 1e Night Horrors: Grimm Fears we are introduced to the character of DJ Hamlyn, who captures captures vampires, werewolves, and mages to give to his keeper. At first, I simply began thinking of kiths that could be made from other supernaturals, but then I began wondering of other avenues for crossover. This could include <i>Faerie Doctors</i>; Fae-touched and ensorcelled humans who awakened as mages, due to their experiences in Faerie, or Pure tribe werewolves whose totem is actually one of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> I would also like to see how much Changelings know about other supernaturals and the interactions between the different societies. How do the vampire organizations of Lancea Sanctum and the Circle of the Crone look at Changelings? Does the Lancea Sanctum view the true Fae as devils and changelings as pagan/heathen souls.<br /> <br /> Does the Autumn Court have diplomatic relations with Geists/Mages/ and Prometheans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:15:24-07:00","id":972710,"title":"","content":"There is a Crossover Chronicle planned, so its seems like you'll get your wish.<br /> <br /> I think any fae touched would most like awaken as Acathus, followed by a minority of Magistos. A residue ability to see the mask and not just enter, but exist the Hedge would be a reasonable, not over powered legacy. If Fae Touch can awaked at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:23:29-07:00","id":972713,"title":"","content":"What do The True Fae think of vampires? In 1e there was an implication that vampires were sometimes spirited away by the True Fae, but in my head, I think the True Fae would regard vampires the same way humans look at rats or cockroaches, because they gave up the most precious part of themselves (their souls) for power and a false immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:28:27-07:00","id":972719,"title":"","content":"The idea of Fae-touched becoming mages was inspired by the legends of Fairy doctors, who are a part of traditional Irish folklore. Here is a definition of the difference between witches and fairy doctors.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:32px\"><b>WITCHES, FAIRY DOCTORS</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Witches and fairy doctors receive their power from opposite dynasties; the witch from evil spirits and her own malignant will; the fairy doctor from the fairies,, and a something--a temperament--that is born with him or her. The first is always feared and hated. The second is gone to for advice, and is never worse than mischievous. The most celebrated fairy doctors are sometimes people the fairies loved and carried away, and kept with them for seven years; not that those the fairies' love are always carried off--they may merely grow silent and strange, and take to lonely wanderings in the &quot;gentle&quot; places. Such will, in after-times, be great poets or musicians, or fairy doctors; they must not be confused with those who have a <i>Lianhaun shee</i> [<i>leann\u00e1n-sidhe</i>], for the <i>Lianhaun shee</i> lives upon the vitals of its chosen, and they waste and die. She is of the dreadful solitary fairies. To her have belonged the greatest of the Irish poets, from Oisin down to the last century.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:11:31-07:00","id":972831,"title":"","content":"In a previous post, I stated that I did not believe True Fae would spirit away vampires, because of their disgust for vampires sacrificing their souls for power and a false immortality. However, in traditional folklore, there are vampires that share the vampire quality of drinking human blood. Along with redcaps, there was the <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Baobhan sith and Glaistig. As such, I think if a crossover Changeling book comes out, they should include a kith that drinks blood like a vampire. Instead of using vampires, the True Fae could use ghouls and dhampires.</span></span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:08:17-07:00","id":972851,"title":"","content":"Maybe the True Fae use vampires as parts and ingredients when making Leechfingers, which would explain why their abilities have simularities.<br /> <br /> I've never heard of Fairy Doctors before, says interrsting, but they do have a Chirgeon Kith, so make of that what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}